Track 1: Skillets Bite the Frost
- Story & Context: During a sub-zero power cut at Tromsø's Old Fish Hall 4, guitarist Torstein Eide dragged an iron skillet across an exposed 240-volt generator terminal, throwing blinding sparks into a tub of beef tallow to jump-start their frozen PA system. The sudden surge kicked the modular synth into a groaning, dead-slow pulse that mimicked the eight-beat-per-minute winter torpor of a sleeping polar bear, until Torstein's fuzz-caked guitar slammed the room back into a 140-BPM riot. Sigrid and the rogue choir shrieked over the howling feedback, defying the Arctic police who were already pounding on the rusted steel loading doors. The opening track documents that frozen flashpoint with the snarling, triumphant hook: "Scrape the grease clean, we are waking from the dead!"
