Track 2: Did You Save a Bowl for Maren?
- Story & Context: Penned after bassist Malin Skog spent three days bunkered in a snowed-in pantry subsisting on boiled barley and diesel-warmed tea, this track is an intimate, bitter confession of isolation turning into collective fury. Malin tracked her basslines through a blown 30-watt practice amp caked in dried flour while Dahl tuned his trance supersaws to the sluggish, irregular respiration of a hibernating ground squirrel. The conflict peaked when a landlord tried to padlock the pantry door, prompting Malin to smash the lock open with a soup ladle while screaming the choir-backed refrain into an open telephone receiver. The recording captures the smell of burnt porridge and raw adrenaline, crowned by the defiant shout: "Count the spoons at the table before you lock us in!"
