Track 3: Sidechain the Winter Sourdough
- Story & Context: The final anthem was recorded during the mythic "St. Lucia Riot" at the docks of Grøtsund, where the band mixed their tracks live using sourdough crocks as acoustic dampening baffles around the drum kit. As the harbor patrol deployed sound cannons across the water to break up the dockside gathering, the choir matched the sirens note for note while the kick drum ducked the entire mix into agonizing, suspended torpor-pauses before releasing into an overwhelming major-key synth explosion. The resulting wave of sound shook rime from the trawler rigging and sent the patrol boats retreating into the blizzard. The track immortalized the standoff with its soaring, euphoric choral chorus: "Knead the bread in the dark, let the fury rise!"
